    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Missing export in governance module** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` but it wasn't being exported from the module\n\n**2. Toxicity metric signature mismatch** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - Updated `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references = [], bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`\n   - The `runEvaluations` function calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` was expecting `bannedTerms` as its second parameter\n   - This caused references to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging safe outputs as toxic\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, and all public exports remain intact:\n- **Governance module**: exports functions + constants\n- **Eval module**: exports functions + metrics",
